  - name: "Summon and Control Totem Sea Creature"
    description: "The ONLY sea druid ability that works like a spell: 20 P.P.E., a one mile (1.6 km) radius, one hour per level of experience, no saving throw. It summons and controls one - and only one - totem creature within range; if none is in range the P.P.E. is wasted, which is why most druids pick a common animal. The creature obeys completely, communicates by a kind of telepathy and empathy, defends the druid and will carry it. It never attacks the druid even when the spell is not in force. The two may separate by up to a mile; beyond that the spell breaks and the creature is free to go."
extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 61-63. The surface dweller''s version of ocean magic -
    passive and defensive where the ocean wizard is not, and the only class in
    this book with a stated racial restriction.
  - ITS SPELL GRANT IS A CHOICE THE APP CANNOT OFFER, and this is the one place
    the modelling loses something real. Printed 63 item 7 gives the druid "any
    two ocean magic or dolphin spells per level of experience OR one Whale
    Singer''s spellsong". A schedule entry draws from ONE list with ONE count, so
    it cannot offer two-from-A-or-one-from-B. The two-spell branch is stored
    because it is the larger grant and the one the class is built around; the
    spellsong alternative is in the starting group''s note and in this list. A
    player taking the spellsong swaps by hand.
  - THE OCEAN AND DOLPHIN LISTS ARE MERGED INTO ONE, because the book offers
    them as a single pool - "any two ocean magic or dolphin spells" - rather
    than two separate grants. That is the honest reading of the sentence and it
    is what makes the schedule expressible at all.
  - `magic.type` IS "druid" RATHER THAN "spell". The type is a KIND rather than
    a ladder, and this class is the book''s druid; the key exists for exactly
    this.
  - IT GETS NO HAND TO HAND SKILL AT ALL. Checked against printed 62 twice
    rather than assumed to be an OCR drop: the O.C.C. skill list runs from Basic
    Math to "One W.P. of choice" and stops. Recorded so the absence reads as
    deliberate.
  - ITS RELATED-SKILL SCHEDULE GIVES TWO PER STEP, not one. Printed 62 says
    "plus two additional skills at levels three, seven, eleven and fifteen",
    where every other caster in this book gives one. Transcribed as printed.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so it needs a `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS` entry.
    1D6: a caster with no hand to hand at all.
