# Sea Druid

## Lore

Sea druids are surface dwellers who treat water as the valuable resource it is and build their lives around it. They do not particularly want to change the environment; they prefer to work with it. Their skills and abilities are passive and defensive by nature, and they alter the natural flow of water only to protect or improve the lives of others - and even then only temporarily.

Each sea druid chooses a common sea creature as a totem animal and can become it at will, gaining all its abilities. The totem can never be a supernatural sea monster or a creature of magic.

They do not value money or possessions nearly as much as they value nature itself.

## GM Notes

A sea druid is an excellent source of information once befriended. They are sensitive to their surroundings and capable of knowing everything going on in the immediate water environment - which of their nine abilities is doing the knowing depends on what you ask.

Most pick a reasonably common totem so the summoning is not wasted: large fish such as the sailfish, barracuda, shark, manta and sting ray, giant squid and octopus, eel, sea snake, marine iguana, sea turtle, sea lion, seal, walrus, sea otter, polar bear, and various common mutants, monsters and D-bee animals. Most dolphins, porpoises and whales are too intelligent to be summoned by this magic at all.

Equipment is deliberately sparse. A sea druid tends toward loose robes and tunics or light clothing, may wear light armour, and relies on magic instead - heavy armour would negate the point of swimming underwater and turning into a totem animal.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sea-druid');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sea-druid';
SELECT count(*) AS stub_gear FROM gear WHERE slug IN ('scaling-knife', 'fishing-pole', 'fishing-hooks-and-lures', 'fishing-net-small');

